# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
scripts/email-mcp-secrets.local.txt

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Ops dashboard — separate private repo; deploys via its own Worker, not Pages build
/groundswell-monitor/

# Large Exports
Jason_Carroll_Holloway_Final_Export/
website_unzipped/
business_cards/
*.pdf
*.epub
*.zip
*_out.txt
*.py

# Python bytecode is never source. `*.py` above never matched .pyc, so these
# caches were fully trackable and one `git add -A` away from being committed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Print/EPUB build scripts MUST be tracked. The blanket `*.py` above hid this
# whole directory; scripts were force-added past it one at a time, and
# audit_body_italics.py -- the Section 5 body-italic shipping gate -- was never
# added, stayed invisible to git, and was lost when the folder was copied in.
# Scoped to this one directory (and non-recursive, since `*` does not cross `/`)
# so virtualenvs, node_modules and caches elsewhere stay ignored.
!production_staging/_scripts_from_windows/*.py

# Web-deliverable public assets — these MUST be tracked or they 404 in production.
# Cloudflare Pages builds from git, so anything untracked never reaches the deploy.
# Scoped to the two sites' `public/` download directories only; print-production
# binaries (production_staging/, _covers/, MASTER_UPLOAD_FOLDER) stay ignored.
!public/press-kit/*.pdf
!public/downloads/*.pdf
!public/downloads/*.epub
!seventhcitypress/public/press-kit/*.pdf

# Not linked from any page and byte-identical to the tracked author-site copy;
# needs an explicit publish decision before it ships.
seventhcitypress/public/press-kit/PressKit_Agent_Prompt.pdf

# Secret hygiene — login / token / credential console output (added 2026-08-29)
# Seven such logs were committed in 32fedf6 on 2026-08-05 and reached origin.
# Their contents are only an OAuth authorize URL with an already-spent PKCE
# challenge, no live credential, so history is deliberately NOT being rewritten
# and the seven are deliberately NOT being `git rm --cached`ed. These rules exist
# only so a FUTURE login run cannot become trackable and get swept in by
# `git add -A`. Scoped to scratch/ops/ so ordinary logs elsewhere are unaffected.
# Do not add a negation for these patterns.
#
# `**/` here matches zero or more directories, so each rule covers both
# scratch/ops/ itself and any subdirectory beneath it.
scratch/ops/**/_wrangler_login*
scratch/ops/**/_*login*
scratch/ops/**/_*token*
scratch/ops/**/_*credential*
scratch/ops/**/_*secret*
scratch/ops/**/_*oauth*
scratch/ops/**/_*api_key*
scratch/ops/**/_*apikey*
scratch/ops/**/_*bearer*
scratch/ops/**/*.pem

# Site-side build / sync / generation scripts MUST be tracked, for exactly the
# reason the print scripts above must be. The negation above was scoped to one
# directory and this one was not in it, so on 2026-08-29 generate_press_kit.py
# was rewritten to read page counts from lib/data/ingram-catalog.json and
# `git diff` reported nothing at all. sync-ingram-metadata.py, which WRITES that
# catalog, was in the same position. Non-recursive, so scripts/__pycache__/ and
# any virtualenv beneath scripts/ stay ignored.
!scripts/*.py

# ...except the one-off social-ops drivers. Every scripts/*.py whose name starts
# with `_` is a single-run Playwright or API cleanup driver written for one
# evening's work (Meta post deletion, X timeline purges, IG caption probes).
# They are history, not tooling. A script that is meant to be re-run must NOT be
# given a leading underscore, or this rule will hide it.
scripts/_*.py

# Cartographer regeneration driver and its two verifiers. These encode the
# "trap 2" input-path rule from cartographer/REGEN_2026-08-29.md: running
# phase1_normalize.mjs against its hardcoded default input silently reverts 39
# geographic corrections. The .mjs phase scripts beside them are already
# tracked; the Python that records how to invoke them safely is not.
!cartographer/*.py

# Name-migration rule sets and their re-runnable regression checks, cited by
# path in production_staging/NAME_FIX_2026-08-29.md as the authoritative record
# of what changed in the prose and how to re-verify it. Non-recursive, so the
# print binaries under production_staging/*/ stay ignored.
!production_staging/*.py

# EPUB/PDF porter verifiers. Both were force-added past the blanket `*.py` and
# are tracked today, so this makes no file newly visible -- it only stops them
# from being one `git rm --cached` or one bad copy away from invisible again.
!production_staging/_docs/*.py

# Press-kit verification toolkit, including prove_gate.py, which corrupts a
# generator, runs the real prebuild command, and proves the gate fails -- the
# only proof that scripts/check-page-counts.mjs catches a stale page count.
# Scoped to this one directory; the rest of scratch/ stays ignored.
!scratch/_press_tools/*.py

# Key-rotation tooling for a Worker directory that is otherwise tracked.
# No credentials are embedded; both scripts read from `gh` and the environment.
!the-bridge-worker/*.py

# Single-run undo copies — `.bak` files expire on commit (added 2026-08-29)
# Every one of these is written by a script immediately before it overwrites
# something, so that one run can be reversed if it goes wrong. Once the change is
# committed the copy has no remaining value: git history IS the durable undo, and
# a `.bak` sitting beside the file is a worse version of it that no tooling reads.
# 204 of them were untracked tonight and one `git add -A` away from putting
# 45.8 MB into clone history permanently — 81% of the untracked payload.
#
# `.pdf.PRE_*.bak` and `.epub.PRE_*.bak` under production_staging/ are why this
# rule is load-bearing rather than merely tidy. They are print binaries that the
# `*.pdf` and `*.epub` rules above already intend to exclude, and they slipped
# past those rules purely because of the trailing `.bak`. The twelve largest
# untracked files in the repo are all of this kind. This rule closes that hole.
#
# Ignoring is the goal, not cleaning — do NOT delete what this hides. The `.bak`
# copies under groundswell-monitor/ are the only copy of anything superseded
# there, because that directory is ignored above and has no git history of its own.
*.bak

# kc-events/ — extracted to its own git repository (added 2026-08-30)
# A complete event-discovery application: 39 Python modules covering ingest
# adapters, dedup, scoring, discovery, a SQLite layer, a CLI, a weekly runner
# and a local dashboard. The blanket `*.py` above hid every one of them, so
# this repo tracked 24 files — configs, README, seed data, reports — and none
# of the program. Copying the folder would have kept the settings and lost the
# application, which is why it now has history of its own.
#
# It is a nested repository at kc-events/.git with one initial commit of 78
# files. Python source is tracked by default there; that inversion is the point.
# This rule stops the trilogy repo from re-absorbing it as an embedded gitlink.
/kc-events/
